            <ArticleTitle>Erosive pustular dermatosis of the scalp after aplasia cutis congenita in a 9-year-old patient: A 5-year follow-up.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>695-696</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/pde.13252</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Erosive pustular dermatosis of the scalp (EPDS) is a rare inflammatory skin disease that occurs mainly in elderly adults with a history of trauma to the scalp, but a few cases of EPDS in children have been reported. We report a rare case of EPDS after aplasia cutis congenita in a child.</AbstractText>
